{"author": "careerwithvasanth", "category": "youtube", "content": {"constraints": [], "context_unit_ids": ["youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540:u000009", "youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540:u000010", "youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540:u000011", "youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540:u000012"], "exceptions": [], "goal": null, "kind": "claim", "prerequisites": [], "steps": [], "summary": {"citations": [{"quote": "the ML models need not to always run on the back end. There are ways now we can run the ML models on the client.", "unit_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540:u000009"}, {"quote": "what if you had a small tensorflow algorithm that runs an ML algorithm that runs on the client and can like predict, okay?", "unit_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540:u000012"}], "text": "Machine learning models can now run on the client side, not just the back end, particularly for smaller user requirements."}, "title": "Running ML models on client-side", "topic": "AI and React"}, "content_hash": "632855d6828747375fb731a549a72a1b9c3737ebd5a5ad99e60532dd2126b8e0", "external_status": "not_checked", "extraction_scope": "source_excerpt", "id": "youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540:knowledge:aed844d528b38314", "metadata_hash": "1ca0057b225667adf07ad07b38dd6a31ef28a116a44a0135a7c9ac292acfb39b", "product": "knowledge", "published_at": "2025-02-08", "semantic_status": "not_reviewed", "source_format": "transcript", "source_hash": "23383070dfd59b7f6127f078a0a36538a4f65e658e7fe9bc9a187742dd854475", "source_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540", "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bLfD_-Fvjas", "title": "Running ML models on client-side", "topic": "AI and React", "topic_slug": "ai-and-react"}
{"author": "careerwithvasanth", "category": "youtube", "content": {"constraints": [], "context_unit_ids": ["youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540:u000013"], "exceptions": [], "goal": null, "kind": "claim", "prerequisites": [], "steps": [], "summary": {"citations": [{"quote": "TensorFlow as you all know like primarily deals with ML algorithm. So they have this JavaScript driven algorithms which can technically run on the browser for a smaller set of inputs and give relatively better results.", "unit_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540:u000013"}], "text": "TensorFlow.js provides JavaScript-driven algorithms that can run on the browser for smaller inputs, aiding personalization."}, "title": "Using TensorFlow.js for Client-Side ML", "topic": "AI and React"}, "content_hash": "632855d6828747375fb731a549a72a1b9c3737ebd5a5ad99e60532dd2126b8e0", "external_status": "not_checked", "extraction_scope": "source_excerpt", "id": "youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540:knowledge:0f0b5e8d261d9ec4", "metadata_hash": "1ca0057b225667adf07ad07b38dd6a31ef28a116a44a0135a7c9ac292acfb39b", "product": "knowledge", "published_at": "2025-02-08", "semantic_status": "not_reviewed", "source_format": "transcript", "source_hash": "23383070dfd59b7f6127f078a0a36538a4f65e658e7fe9bc9a187742dd854475", "source_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540", "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bLfD_-Fvjas", "title": "Using TensorFlow.js for Client-Side ML", "topic": "AI and React", "topic_slug": "ai-and-react"}
{"author": "careerwithvasanth", "category": "youtube", "content": {"constraints": [], "context_unit_ids": ["youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540:u000025", "youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540:u000026", "youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540:u000027", "youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540:u000028", "youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540:u000029"], "exceptions": [], "goal": null, "kind": "advice", "prerequisites": [], "steps": [], "summary": {"citations": [{"quote": "we no longer gonna have the same set of AI which was like running on the back end. We start having the AI models running on the client.", "unit_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540:u000025"}, {"quote": "I'll just summarize the video. So where we all have to start thinking about AI first in React. So how do we embed AI models into React Native or React JS.", "unit_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540:u000029"}], "text": "We need to start thinking about embedding AI models into React Native or React JS along with the backend."}, "title": "AI integration into React explained", "topic": "AI and React"}, "content_hash": "632855d6828747375fb731a549a72a1b9c3737ebd5a5ad99e60532dd2126b8e0", "external_status": "not_checked", "extraction_scope": "source_excerpt", "id": "youtube-video-2025-02-08-react-ai-the-future-of-frontend-development-blfd-fvjas-md-043ec20540:knowledge:698d4990744c09ce", "metadata_hash": "1ca0057b225667adf07ad07b38dd6a31ef28a116a44a0135a7c9ac292acfb39b", "product": "knowledge", "published_at": "2025-02-08", "semantic_status": "not_reviewed", "source_format": "transcript", "source_hash": "233830